      "text": "## The Big Picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-VENTILATION.md#002",
      "path": [
        "06-VENTILATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:hvac:06-ventilation, git-history:hvac:06-ventilation]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/06-VENTILATION.md",
        "concepts": "[ventilation]",
        "current_path": "hvac/06-VENTILATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ventilation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ventilation]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ventilation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Modern tight construction created a new problem: buildings no longer breathe enough\nto maintain acceptable indoor air quality by accident. Intentional mechanical ventilation\nis now required — and the energy cost of ventilating can be recovered through heat exchange."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-VENTILATION.md#003",
      "path": [
        "06-VENTILATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:hvac:06-ventilation, git-history:hvac:06-ventilation]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/06-VENTILATION.md",
        "concepts": "[ventilation]",
        "current_path": "hvac/06-VENTILATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ventilation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ventilation]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ventilation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|               THE TIGHT BUILDING DILEMMA                             |\n|                                                                      |\n|  OLD LEAKY HOUSE           NEW TIGHT HOUSE                           |\n|  (>10 ACH50)               (<3 ACH50)                                |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Natural infiltration      Minimal infiltration                      |\n|  keeps air \"fresh\"         saves energy                              |\n|  (accidentally)            BUT indoor air quality                    |\n|                            degrades without                          |\n|  Large heating/cooling     intentional ventilation                   |\n|  energy waste                                                        |\n|                            Solution: mechanical                      |\n|  No mold risk from         ventilation with                          |\n|  tight air pockets         energy recovery                           |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n         |                                    |\n         v                                    v\n  Rule: tighter is better for energy;  tighter requires ventilation\n  build tight, ventilate right\n```"
    },
